  "semanticReview": [
    {
      "topic": "Empty viewport only",
      "conclusion": "The fallback is entered only for the formerly dead nearest-scrollport branch with a nonzero target. The original positive branch and wheel loop are byte-identical; a fallback result cannot satisfy target readiness."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Clipping and owner",
      "conclusion": "The exposed candidate rectangle is clipped by the viewport and every clipping ancestor on the relevant axes. Non-scrollable intermediate clips constrain the reveal rectangle. The single center hit must be in the candidate and resolve from the hit itself to that exact nearest vertical owner; foreign overlays or nested owners refuse."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Multiple offscreen ports",
      "conclusion": "An unexposed scrolling ancestor becomes the next reveal rectangle. The eventual delta follows that port rather than the originally clipped target contents. Both above-viewport and intermediate-port geometry are discriminated by exact expected deltas in appended actual-expression cases."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Authority and bounds",
      "conclusion": "Only the adjacent outer scrollTo guard is removed. The unchanged waitRead guard remains before every read/retry and next loop iteration. This does not create or claim a new post-evaluate pre-wheel guard. Wheel/read budgets, timing, exception behavior and all other controls remain exact."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Regression meaning",
      "conclusion": "The complete old162195-byte suite remains a prefix. Appended fixtures execute the real generated expression, change geometry only after recorded wheel commands, assert exact command/step/guard sequences, exercise twelve refusals and preserve the final-read budget. These are reviewed source assertions, not executed passes."
